    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A northern Thai kingdom founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangrai">Mangrai</a>, who took Hariphunchai and built Chiang Mai as his capital in 1296.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tilokarat">Tilokarat</a> in the fifteenth century it fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> and became a leading centre of Pali Buddhist learning.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> ruled it for most of 1558–1775, after which its principalities passed under Siam.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha">Emerald Buddha</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>'s most sacred image, was kept in Chiang Mai from 1468 until the early 1550s, when it was taken to Lan Xang.</p></aside>
    </section>

